;; Task registry for `nbb scripts/run-task.cljs <task> [args…]` (ADR-2607173000).
;;
;; Until 2026-08-13 this file was NOT a conversion but a facade:
;;   {:test {:cmd ["bb" "test"]} :seed-dry-run {:cmd ["bb" "seed-dry-run"]}}
;; The nbb registry shelled straight back out to the binary ADR-2607173000
;; retired, and bb.edn was still present as the real definition. It passed on
;; this laptop only because bb happens to sit in ~/.local/bin; on a murakumo
;; fleet node — none of which has bb — every task here failed to start.
;; bb.edn is now gone and these are the real invocations (ADR-2608133200).
{:test
 {:cmd ["clojure" "-M:test" "run_tests.clj"]
  :doc "Run the 12 standalone kuni-umi suites listed in run_tests.clj (cells, kotoba ingest, repository contract, robotics). Exits 1 when any suite fails, so it is usable as a gate."}

 :seed-dry-run
 {:cmd ["clojure" "-M" "-m" "kuni-umi.kotoba.ingest-mcp" "--dry-run"]
  :pass-args? true
  :doc "Parse kotoba/seed.edn and report entity/datom counts without writing anything. --dry-run is passed explicitly rather than relying on the default, so the task cannot become a live ingest if that default ever changes. Extra args are forwarded: --url / --graph."}}
